# NOT ignored: /android/, /ios/, /web/, analysis_options.yaml, pubspec.lock.
#
# They were excluded here while the project was being worked on in an
# environment that had no Flutter SDK and therefore none of those files. That
# was wrong for a real repository:
#
#   * android/ holds the manifest -- the INTERNET permission and the cleartext
#     setting -- and the Gradle config. Excluded, a fresh clone does not build
#     and those two settings exist only on one laptop.
#   * analysis_options.yaml configures the linter that `flutter analyze` runs,
#     so without it the same code reports different problems to different
#     people.
#   * pubspec.lock pins the exact dependency versions. Flutter's own guidance
#     is to commit it for an application, so a build in two months resolves
#     the same packages as a build today.
#
# `flutter create` writes an android/.gitignore of its own which excludes the
# machine-specific parts (local.properties, the Gradle cache, keystores), so
# those stay out without keeping the whole folder out.
/.metadata

